th","designation":"Epsilon Ursae Majoris","ra":193.5073,"dec":55.9598,"magnitude":1.76,"ci":-0.022},{"name":"Mizar","designation":"Zeta Ursae Majoris","ra":200.9814,"dec":54.9254,"magnitude":2.23,"ci":0.057},{"name":"Alkaid","designation":"Eta Ursae Majoris","ra":206.8852,"dec":49.3133,"magnitude":1.86,"ci":-0.099}],"lines":[["Dubhe","Merak"],["Merak","Phecda"],["Phecda","Megrez"],["Megrez","Dubhe"],["Megrez","Alioth"],["Alioth","Mizar"],["Mizar","Alkaid"]],"mythology":"In Greek myth the nymph Callisto was turned into a bear, by Hera in jealousy or by Zeus to hide her. Years later her son Arcas, out hunting, nearly killed her; Zeus swept both into the sky as the Great Bear and the Little Bear."},"Ursa Minor":{"abbreviation":"UMi","stars":[{"name":"Polaris","designation":"Alpha Ursae Minoris","ra":37.9546,"dec":89.2641,"magnitude":1.98,"ci":0.636},{"name":"Yildun","designation":"Delta Ursae Minoris","ra":263.0539,"dec":86.5864,"magnitude":4.35,"ci":0.021},{"name":"Epsilon Ursae Minoris","designation":"Epsilon Ursae Minoris","ra":251.4927,"dec":82.0373,"magnitude":4.21,"ci":0.897},{"name":"Zeta Ursae Minoris","designation":"Zeta Ursae Minoris","ra":236.0147,"dec":77.7945,"magnitude":4.32,"ci":0.038},{"name":"Kochab","designation":"Beta Ursae Minoris","ra":222.6764,"dec":74.1555,"magnitude":2.08,"ci":1.465},{"name":"Pherkad","designation":"Gamma Ursae Minoris","ra":230.1822,"dec":71.834,"magnitude":3.0,"ci":0.058},{"name":"Eta Ursae Minoris","designation":"Eta Ursae Minoris","ra":244.3761,"dec":75.7553,"magnitude":4.95,"ci":0.393}],"lines":[["Polaris","Yildun"],["Yildun","Epsilon Ursae Minoris"],["Epsilon Ursae Minoris","Zeta Ursae Minoris"],["Zeta Ursae Minoris","Kochab"],["Zeta Ursae Minoris","Eta Ursae Minoris"],["Eta Ursae Minoris","Pherkad"],["Pherkad","Kochab"]],"mythology":"The Little Bear is usually identified with Arcas, son of Callisto, placed in the sky beside his mother. Another story says it honours Ida, one of the nymphs who cared for the infant Zeus on Crete."},"Cassiopeia":{"abbreviation":"Cas","stars":[{"name":"Caph","designation":"Beta Cassiopeiae","ra":2.2945,"dec":59.1498,"magnitude":2.28,"ci":0.38},{"name":"Schedar","designation":"Alpha Cassiopeiae","ra":10.1268,"dec":56.5373,"magnitude":2.24,"ci":1.17},{"name":"Gamma Cassiopeiae","designation":"Gamma Cassiopeiae","ra":14.1772,"dec":60.7167,"magnitude":2.15,"ci":-0.046},{"name":"Ruchbah","designation":"Delta Cassiopeiae","ra":21.454,"dec":60.2353,"magnitude":2.68,"ci":0.16},{"name":"Segin","designation":"Epsilon Cassiopeiae","ra":28.5989,"dec":63.6701,"magnitude":3.38,"ci":-0.15}],"lines":[["Caph","Schedar"],["Schedar","Gamma Cassiopeiae"],["Gamma Cassiopeiae","Ruchbah"],["Ruchbah","Segin"]],"mythology":"Cassiopeia was a vain queen of Aethiopia who boasted that she (or her daughter Andromeda) was more beautiful than the sea nymphs. As punishment, Poseidon sent a sea monster, and Cassiopeia was set in the sky on her throne, circling the pole and spending half the night upside down."},"Leo":{"abbreviation":"Leo","stars":[{"name":"Regulus","designation":"Alpha Leonis","ra":152.093,"dec":11.9672,"magnitude":1.35,"ci":-0.087},{"name":"Denebola","designation":"Beta Leonis","ra":177.2649,"dec":14.5721,"magnitude":2.14,"ci":0.09},{"name":"Algieba","designation":"Gamma Leonis","ra":154.9931,"dec":19.8415,"magnitude":2.08,"ci":1.128},{"name":"Zosma","designation":"Delta Leonis","ra":168.5271,"dec":20.5238,"magnitude":2.56,"ci":0.128},{"name":"Epsilon Leonis","designation":"Epsilon Leonis","ra":146.4628,"dec":23.7743,"magnitude":2.98,"ci":0.808},{"name":"Mu Leonis","designation":"Mu Leonis","ra":148.1909,"dec":26.007,"magnitude":3.88,"ci":1.222},{"name":"Zeta Leonis","designation":"Zeta Leonis","ra":154.1726,"dec":23.4173,"magnitude":3.43,"ci":0.307},{"name":"Eta Leonis","designation":"Eta Leonis","ra":151.8331,"dec":16.7627,"magnitude":3.48,"ci":-0.031},{"name":"Theta Leonis","designation":"Theta Leonis","ra":168.56,"dec":15.4296,"magnitude":3.33,"ci":-0.003}],"lines":[["Epsilon Leonis","Mu Leonis"],["Mu Leonis","Zeta Leonis"],["Zeta Leonis","Algieba"],["Algieba","Eta Leonis"],["Eta Leonis","Regulus"],["Algieba","Zosma"],["Zosma","Denebola"],["Regulus","Theta Leonis"],["Theta Leonis","Denebola"]],"mythology":"Leo is the Nemean Lion, a beast whose golden hide no weapon could pierce. Slaying it was the first of the twelve labours of Heracles, who strangled the lion and afterwards wore its skin as armour."},"Scorpius":{"abbreviation":"Sco","stars":[{"name":"Antares","designation":"Alpha Scorpii","ra":247.3519,"dec":-26.432,"magnitude":1.06,"ci":1.865},{"name":"Shaula","designation":"Lambda Scorpii","ra":263.4022,"dec":-37.1038,"magnitude":1.62,"ci":-0.231},{"name":"Sargas","designation":"Theta Scorpii","ra":264.3297,"dec":-42.9978,"magnitude":1.86,"ci":0.406},{"name":"Dschubba","designation":"Delta Scorpii","ra":240.0834,"dec":-22.6217,"magnitude":2.32,"ci":-0.117},{"name":"Acrab","designation":"Beta Scorpii","ra":241.3593,"dec":-19.8055,"magnitude":2.62,"ci":-0.065},{"name":"Pi Scorpii","designation":"Pi Scorpii","ra":239.713,"dec":-26.1141,"magnitude":2.89,"ci":-0.18},{"name":"Epsilon Scorpii","designation":"Epsilon Scorpii","ra":252.5425,"dec":-34.2933,"magnitude":2.29,"ci":1.144},{"name":"Kappa Scorpii","designation":"Kappa Scorpii","ra":265.622,"dec":-39.03,"magnitude":2.39,"ci":-0.171},{"name":"Lesath","designation":"Upsilon Scorpii","ra":262.691,"dec":-37.2958,"magnitude":2.69,"ci":-0.179}],"lines":[["Acrab","Dschubba"],["Dschubba","Pi Scorpii"],["Dschubba","Antares"],["Antares","Epsilon Scorpii"],["Epsilon Scorpii","Sargas"],["Sargas","Kappa Scorpii"],["Kappa Scorpii","Shaula"],["Shaula","Lesath"]],"mythology":"Scorpius is the scorpion sent by Gaia to kill the boastful hunter Orion. The two were placed on opposite sides of the sky, so the scorpion rises in the east as Orion sets in the west — they are never seen together."},"Cygnus":{"abbreviation":"Cyg","stars":[{"name":"Deneb","designation":"Alpha Cygni","ra":310.358,"dec"